From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: enable the RK356x/RK3588 crypto
 offloader

CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP2 is a tristate with no default, so the driver the
preceding patches add is never built by a kernel whose config comes from
the in-tree arm64 defconfig -- the DT nodes describe a device nothing
binds to.  No kconfig fragment in this collection sets it either, so this
is the only place it can come from.

Set it =m, next to CRYPTO_DEV_QCOM_RNG and CRYPTO_DEV_TEGRA where
savedefconfig orders it, and matching every other SoC crypto offloader in
the file.

This hunk is ours, not part of the upstream series, and it is the reason
the series is worth applying at all in a default build.  Drop it if a
consumer supplies its own kconfig fragment for the same symbol.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 96ce783f2..c9991b95d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -1955,6 +1955,7 @@ CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_FSL_CAAM=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_FSL_DPAA2_CAAM=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCE=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCOM_RNG=m
+CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP2=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_TEGRA=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_XILINX_TRNG=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_ZYNQMP_AES=m
